# BirdNote

Native Android app that helps users get better at reading sheet music and recognizing notes on a staff. Prefer practice over theory dumps or a sheet-music editor.

## Product

- Goal: improve note reading and staff recognition. How users practice is still open; do not lock in a specific drill, quiz, or curriculum unless asked.
- Keep the UI mobile-first and easy to use on a phone. Prefer clear notation over dense score layouts.
- Offline-first; no backend unless explicitly requested.

## Stack

- Language: Kotlin (`kotlin.code.style=official`), Java 11 bytecode
- UI: Jetpack Compose + Material 3 (`BirdNoteTheme`), not Views/XML layouts
- Entry: single-module `:app`, package `com.example.birdnote`, launcher `MainActivity`
- Build: Gradle version catalog (`gradle/libs.versions.toml`), AGP 9.4.1, Kotlin 2.2.10, Compose BOM
- SDK: `minSdk 26`, `compileSdk`/`targetSdk` 37
- Tests: JUnit 4 unit tests; Espresso + Compose UI tests for instrumented